sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/active-inference-morphogenesis-falsifiable--claude-opus-5-5--1> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Lean: a finite complete-class theorem showing exactly when free-energy accounts are empty" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/active-inference-morphogenesis-falsifiable> ;
    dct:description "Make the unfalsifiability charge precise, which is a result in itself. Setting: finite hidden-state space S, finite observations O, finite actions A, and a policy π: Oⁿ → A over a finite horizon. Theorem 1 (finite complete class): for every deterministic policy π there exist a generative model (prior over S, likelihood, and preference prior over outcomes) under which π minimizes expected free energy; the construction places preference mass on the outcomes π produces. So without constraints on the generative model, the claim 'morphogenesis minimizes free energy' excludes no behaviour. Theorem 2 (restoring content): if the likelihood and preference prior are fixed in advance (for example the target morphology and the cell-signalling likelihood from Friston et al. 2015's model), the set of free-energy-optimal policies is a proper subset, and there exist observable trajectories outside it, with an explicit separating example. This gives a formal criterion: an active-inference morphogenesis claim is testable iff it fixes the components named in Theorem 2." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Lean-checked Theorems 1 and 2. Together they state precisely that the framework is empty with a free generative model and testable with a fixed one, which turns the falsifiability debate into a checkable criterion that approaches 2 and 3 then meet." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: Expected free energy has several non-equivalent definitions in the literature, and the theorems hold for one but not others; the result then must be stated per definition, which weakens its reach." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/formalization" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Define finite POMDP-style generative models and expected free energy over Finset types in Lean. 2. Prove Theorem 1 by explicit construction of the preference prior. 3. Prove Theorem 2 with a small explicit fixed model (for example 3 states, 2 actions) and a trajectory not optimal under it. 4. Write a short note mapping critics' and proponents' statements to Theorems 1 and 2." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): tractable" ;
    skos:note "Tool: lean4" ;
    skos:note "Tool: mathlib" ;
    skos:note "Tool: variational-inference" ;
    skos:note "Tool: philosophy-of-science" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-place-03> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-place-04> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-15> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-girardia-20> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2014.1383> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0015554> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/active-inference-morphogenesis-falsifiable> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "A falsifiable form of active-inference morphogenesis" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2014.1383> dct:title "Knowing one's place: a free-energy approach to pattern regulation" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Friston, Levin, Sengupta and Pezzulo 2015, Knowing one's place" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0015554> dct:title "Observing the Observer (I): Meta-Bayesian Models of Learning and Decision-Making" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Daunizeau et al. 2010, Observing the observer (I): meta-Bayesian models of learning and decision-making (complete class argument)" .
}

